[INFO] [STEP 008] Scientific Context:
[INFO] [STEP 008]   The TEP coupling parameter β quantifies the strength of the conformal coupling
[INFO] [STEP 008]   between matter and the Temporal Topology scalar field. It is determined by fitting
[INFO] [STEP 008]   the predicted velocity anomaly from the scalar force model to the observed
[INFO] [STEP 008]   Doppler measurements from NASA's Deep Space Network.
[INFO] [STEP 008] 
[INFO] [STEP 008] Selection Criterion (a priori, S/N > 2):
[INFO] [STEP 008]   Flybys are included in fitting only if the observed anomaly has signal-to-noise
[INFO] [STEP 008]   ratio ≥ 2. This prevents confirmation bias by excluding marginal detections.
[INFO] [STEP 008]   Current analysis: Will show count after fitting completes.
[INFO] [STEP 008]   Sign agreement at β_ref: not enforced for fitting (strict_sign_gate=false); inverse-variance headline uses all S/N-qualified fits; sign-gated diagnostic is separate.
