[INFO] [STEP 008] Purpose: Verify that TEP framework conclusions are stable against
[INFO] [STEP 008] statistical fluctuations and do not depend on any single flyby.
[INFO] [STEP 008] Three complementary approaches:
[INFO] [STEP 008]   1. Bootstrap resampling - assess uncertainty from small sample size
[INFO] [STEP 008]   2. Leave-one-out cross-validation - test sensitivity to single flyby
[INFO] [STEP 008]   3. Statistical power analysis - evaluate sample size adequacy
[INFO] [STEP 008] 
[INFO] [STEP 008] Method: Parametric bootstrap with n=10,000 iterations addresses the
[INFO] [STEP 008] fundamental limitation of small sample size (n=3 primary detections).
[INFO] [STEP 008] Each iteration resamples with replacement and adds measurement noise.
